<newsitem itemid="114826" id="root" date="1996-10-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: Chrysler Corp Q3 net rises.</title>
<headline>Chrysler Corp Q3 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr primary		$0.93		    $0.45</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$0.93		    $0.45</p>
<p> Net			680,000		  354,000</p>
<p> Revs		  14,356,000	     12,009,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     728,300		  774,500</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     732,300		  787,300</p>
<p>NOTE - 1996 Q3 includes after-tax charge of $55 million, or $0.07/fully diluted share, for voluntary early retirement costs. Results reflect 2-for-1 stock split.  </p>
<p>				  9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr primary		$3.65		    $1.28</p>
<p> Shr diluted		$3.62		    $1.24</p>
<p> Net		    2,722,000		  985,000</p>
<p> Revs		  45,151,000	     38,138,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary     745,600		  752,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs diluted     751,800		  796,900</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>1995 9-month includes after-tax charges of $162 million, or $0.20 per fully diluted share, for production changes at Newark, Del., plant; $96 million, or $0.12/share, for rental car sale accounting change, and $71 million, or $0.09/share, for voluntary minivan service action.</p>
<p>Q3 worldwide factory shipments 650,529 vehicles vs 581,853.</p>
<p>Q3 automotive cash $7.49 billion vs $6.41 billion.</p>
<p>Chrysler Financial Corp Q3 net $94 million vs $87 million.</p>
</text>
